      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "| $x$ | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** | **$6$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-5$ | $2$ | $-3$ | $5$ | $-2$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{3}{x}^{3}$ that best fits the data above can be found using polynomial regression as \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?",
      "worked_solution": "| $x$ | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** | **$6$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-5$ | $2$ | $-3$ | $5$ | $-2$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the curve \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{3}{x}^{3}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & {2}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 3 & {3}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 5 & {5}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 6 & {6}^{3}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
